If the bot bones became so dominant that they were almost
all the bones you'd ever see, that would be annoying.  To
date, I've only seen bot bones once, and I've seen non-bot
bones on a rather larger number of occasions, so I'm not
convinced there's a problem.

The other thing is, exotic bones are a double-edged sword,
and bot bones (in my extremely limited experience -- once
so far) are tame in both respects:  the loot was dull, but the
danger was rather staid as well.  I think the level had, like,
three dingoes (with numeric names) and a peaceful dwarf,
or something like that.  It was actually kind of a relief
when I realized they were bot bones, because the
numerically named monsters had me rather worried,
thinking maybe somebody'd been pudding farming next
to a polymorph trap or somesuch.  The results could've
been rather scary, but it was nothing like that.  The
bot had apparently named every single monster it
encountered, and they were just ordinary mundane
monsters -- a little below average for their depth in
the mine, if anything.

One bones change I'd like to see is the ability
for the game to save more than one set of
bones for the same level -- on loading, then,
it would select one of them at random.  This
would result in a small increase in the number
of bones levels you'd encounter (because, if
somebody dies on a level for which there are
bones already, and they leave bones, the
number of bones files available in total would
increase by one; somebody could still get the
ones that, with the way things are done now,
get overwritten), but more interestingly it would
mean that the bones you would get might not
be from the most recent time somebody died
there.  The bones levels could be loaded out
of order.

That, and wizard bones should only be
loaded in wizard mode, and explore mode
bones should only be loaded in explore
mode.  (Wizard mode bones are irrelevant
on a public server, of course.)

Oh, and when you die on a bones level your
tombstone should indicate that.

Oh, and when somebody on a public server
encounters bones from one of my games,
it would be cool if I could get notified by
email after the fact, with the URL to get
their ttyrec, in case I want to watch it and
see what happened to them.  There have
been a couple of times when I've died and
been left wondering what somebody would
do upon encountering those bones (if the
game saved the bones).  The only possible
downside to this is that it could potentially
lead to bones trolling (deliberate creation
of unusual bones to get a reaction), but
that could be mitigated by letting players
set a pref to opt out of having the previous
player notified after they play through
a bones level.  (There's also already an
option on NAO to not load bones at all.)


